  "explanation": {
    "what": "Plain language: different liver tests show different kinds of damage, and some numbers linger after the damage stops. Scientific terms: unconjugated (indirect) bilirubin, albumin-bound and water-insoluble, is conjugated with glucuronic acid in the liver (direct); diazo reaction is the reference method. R value = (ALT/ULN)/(ALP/ULN): > 5 hepatocellular, 2–5 mixed, < 2 cholestatic. GGT confirms biliary origin of ALP (not raised in bone disease). Delta-bilirubin = conjugated bilirubin covalently bound to albumin.",
    "why": "Hepatocyte injury releases aminotransferases; biliary obstruction induces ALP. Delta-bilirubin adopts albumin’s half-life (17–21 days) and is not filtered, so direct bilirubin falls slowly without bilirubinuria.",
    "measure": "Delta-bilirubin is measured as direct bilirubin and cannot be distinguished from conjugated bilirubin in routine assays. Albumin is a slow, inflammation-sensitive marker; PT/INR reflects factor synthesis.",
    "differs": "Hepatocellular vs cholestatic vs mixed (R value). Direct vs conjugated bilirubin. Alcoholic hepatitis (AST:ALT > 2) vs NAFLD (ALT > AST).",
    "examAngle": "Expect: R value calculation, ALP source questions, direct vs conjugated, prolonged jaundice in recovery, albumin vs PT."
  },
  "comparisons": [
    {
      "id": "hc-ch",
      "title": "Hepatocellular vs cholestatic pattern",
      "left": {
        "label": "Hepatocellular",
        "points": [
          "ALT/AST ↑↑",
          "R > 5"
        ]
      },
      "right": {
        "label": "Cholestatic",
        "points": [
          "ALP ↑↑ (GGT ↑), bilirubin ↑",
          "R < 2"
        ]
      },
      "distinguisher": "R value and which enzyme family dominates."
    },
    {
      "id": "conj-delta",
      "title": "Free conjugated vs delta-bilirubin",
      "left": {
        "label": "Free conjugated",
        "points": [
          "Half-life 2–4 h",
          "Filtered → bilirubinuria"
        ]
      },
      "right": {
        "label": "Delta (albumin-bound)",
        "points": [
          "Half-life 17–21 days",
          "Not filtered; still “direct”"
        ]
      },
      "distinguisher": "Covalent albumin binding."
    }
  ],
  "mnemonic": {
